// hello.loft — the canonical first program.
//
// This whole file IS the program.  A `.loft` file with loose statements is a
// SCRIPT: no `fn main`, no `;` needed between top-level statements, and they
// run once, top to bottom.  Add a `fn main` when you want an explicit entry
// point — both shapes are compiled the same way after that.
//
// Loft has no `let`, no `var`, no type annotations on locals.  You assign a
// value and the compiler infers the type for you.  String interpolation uses
// braces: `"Hello, {name}!"` substitutes the variable.  `print` writes without
// a trailing newline.

name = "world"
print("Hello, {name}!\n")
